# /etc/fstab - the pool's lines on the as-built guest (root, EFI and swap lines omitted).
#
# <XFS_UUID>: blkid -s UUID -o value /dev/mapper/hc680crypt
#
# Options that are load-bearing (see docs/03-guest-storage-stack.md):
#   nofail                          the pool comes up late; boot must not wait for it or fail
#                                   without it. It is also what keeps this mount from being
#                                   ordered before local-fs.target, which would form an
#                                   ordering cycle with the assembly units (After=local-fs.target)
#   x-systemd.requires=...          pull in and wait for the late assembly + unlock chain
#   x-systemd.device-timeout=15min  wait this long for the decrypted device (default is 90 s)
#
# On OpenMediaVault the block between the markers is generated by OMV. Register the
# filesystem in OMV with these options in its "opts" field, or OMV will rewrite the line
# without them (docs/04-openmediavault-and-synology-integration.md). On plain Debian, write
# the first line yourself and leave out the markers.
#
# >>> [openmediavault]
/dev/disk/by-uuid/<XFS_UUID>		/srv/hc680	xfs	defaults,noatime,inode64,nofail,x-systemd.requires=zonedpool-mdassemble.service,x-systemd.requires=zonedpool-cryptopen.service,x-systemd.device-timeout=15min	0 2
/srv/hc680/media/		/export/media	none	bind,nofail	0 0
# <<< [openmediavault]
#
# The second line is the bind mount OMV creates for an NFS export of a shared folder named
# "media" (docs/04). You do not write it by hand on OMV.
